I have renamed the script to myenergy.py and it uses myenergy.env

(octopus) richardhine@Mac homely % ./homely.py --help
usage: homely.py [-h] [--profile PROFILE] [--all-profiles] [--env-file ENV_FILE] [--dry-run] [--today] [--auth-test] [--slots SLOTS]

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit
  --profile PROFILE    Profile name from home_agile.env; defaults to DEFAULT_PROFILE
  --all-profiles       Run every profile found in home_agile.env
  --env-file ENV_FILE  Config file path; default: home_agile.env beside this script
  --dry-run            Show proposed change but do not write the DHW schedule
  --today              Use today's Agile prices rather than tomorrow's
  --auth-test          Test Homely login and dynamic discovery, then exit
  --slots SLOTS        Override number of cheapest half-hour slots


Useful combinations
Safest first test:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard --auth-test
Simulate today's schedule:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard --today --dry-run
Simulate tomorrow's schedule:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard --dry-run
Simulate today using the cheapest six half-hour periods:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard --today --slots 6 --dry-run
Actually update today's Homely schedule:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard --today
Actually update tomorrow's Homely schedule:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py --profile Richard
If DEFAULT_PROFILE=Richard is set in home_agile.env, you can omit --profile Richard, so the normal unattended command is simply:
./homely_agile_dhw_v5_profiles.py
Precedence
For the number of DHW half-hour slots, the script uses:
--slots N
    ↓ if absent
Richard.AGILE_DHW_SLOTS
    ↓ if absent
AGILE_DHW_SLOTS
    ↓ if absent
4
And for the profile:
--profile Richard
    ↓ if absent
DEFAULT_PROFILE
